{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 rulings on 097030b3. Build on main after RC-1 lands, as you\nsay in item 8.\n\nQ1. Yes. Version 2 keeps each version 1 field at the top level.\nThe top-level `meaning` and `envelope` are those of the latest\nsigning. `signings[]` lists every signing with its intent\ndigest, meaning, `notAfter`, `dead` and `closed`. Only an\nearlier signing that is not closed holds an envelope there. The\nlatest envelope is not written twice. The upgrade sits in\n`Custody.#read` alone.\n\nQ2. Agreed. No new format word.\n\nQ3 and Q4. One change makes both small. `byTarget` and the\nchange signal are optional members of the port. C1 gives them\nto `memoryStore` only. `fileStore`, `sqliteStore` and the two\nexample stores do not change: no index directory, no new\ncolumn, no `fs.watch`. No caller of those stores reads by\ntarget. NF-5 gives both members to the browser store. The\nclient of the note takes a store that has both, and its type\nsays so.\n\n`byTarget` takes an identity with no key: service, membership,\nsigner and target. It returns each live record of that\nidentity, whatever its phase, as { id, key, phase, created }.\nThe client drops the records that the replica already holds.\nR2 stands: an archived record is not listed.\n\nQ5. R1: refuse `full`, reason `bytes`, before the signing. That\nreason exists today, so no reason is new. Section 4, item 3: a\n`{ folded: { fact, intent } }` outcome and its `Decided` form\nare accepted. Item 4: `closed?: true` is accepted. Item 5:\n`resign` refuses a record with steps, a standalone record and a\ncreation, with `conflicting`. State in the C1 note that an act\nwith a preparation step takes no second signing. I rule on that\nlimit at C3.\n\nItems 1, 2, 6, 7 and 9 of section 4 are accepted as you state\nthem. R3, R4 and R5 are accepted. R5 goes into NF-5: IndexedDB,\n`navigator.locks` and `BroadcastChannel`.\n\nThe stubs in hosted-tools.test.ts need no new member, because\nboth members are optional.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}